            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yeah, this is possible, but on a more low level. All highlighting is done via extmarks (see `:h extmarks`) in a single namespace (see `:h namespace`). Right now it has name \"MiniHipatternsHighlight\" by which you can get namespace id via `vim.api.nvim_get_namespaces().MiniHipatternsHighlight`. After that, usage built-in tools to get extmarks data should be doable (like calling `:h nvim_buf_get_extmarks()` for every present buffer).\r\n\r\nI think the best approach here would be to fix and \"export\" namespace name to allow this kind of manipulations.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yeah, this is possible, but on a more low level. All highlighting is done via extmarks (see <code class=\"notranslate\">:h extmarks</code>) in a single namespace (see <code class=\"notranslate\">:h namespace</code>). Right now it has name \"MiniHipatternsHighlight\" by which you can get namespace id via <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.api.nvim_get_namespaces().MiniHipatternsHighlight</code>. After that, usage built-in tools to get extmarks data should be doable (like calling <code class=\"notranslate\">:h nvim_buf_get_extmarks()</code> for every present buffer).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I think the best approach here would be to fix and \"export\" namespace name to allow this kind of manipulations.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Yeah, this is possible, but on a more low level. All highlighting is done via extmarks (see :h extmarks) in a single namespace (see :h namespace). Right now it has name \"MiniHipatternsHighlight\" by which you can get namespace id via vim.api.nvim_get_namespaces().MiniHipatternsHighlight. After that, usage built-in tools to get extmarks data should be doable (like calling :h nvim_buf_get_extmarks() for every present buffer).\nI think the best approach here would be to fix and \"export\" namespace name to allow this kind of manipulations.",
