            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "One usecase I imagined for a feature like this is \"hunting\" for todos in the project, e.g. trying to fix all todos before a release or something like that. However this would require a project-wide search (backed by ripgrep or something), which seems like its out of the scope of what `hipatterns` does.\r\n\r\nI'm honestly not sure how something like this could be supported, thoughts?",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">One usecase I imagined for a feature like this is \"hunting\" for todos in the project, e.g. trying to fix all todos before a release or something like that. However this would require a project-wide search (backed by ripgrep or something), which seems like its out of the scope of what <code class=\"notranslate\">hipatterns</code> does.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm honestly not sure how something like this could be supported, thoughts?</p>",
            "bodyText": "One usecase I imagined for a feature like this is \"hunting\" for todos in the project, e.g. trying to fix all todos before a release or something like that. However this would require a project-wide search (backed by ripgrep or something), which seems like its out of the scope of what hipatterns does.\nI'm honestly not sure how something like this could be supported, thoughts?",
