                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Yes, the fact that it doesn't scan all files but only enabled buffers is how 'mini.hipatterns' works (and what initially was the motivation to not implement this). And enabling search in some other buffers is indeed out of scope.\r\n\r\nTo hunt for TODOs in a project, I'd use a good old grepping: either with `MiniPick.builtin.grep()` or `MiniPick.builtin.grep_live()`.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, the fact that it doesn't scan all files but only enabled buffers is how 'mini.hipatterns' works (and what initially was the motivation to not implement this). And enabling search in some other buffers is indeed out of scope.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To hunt for TODOs in a project, I'd use a good old grepping: either with <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.builtin.grep()</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.builtin.grep_live()</code>.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Yes, the fact that it doesn't scan all files but only enabled buffers is how 'mini.hipatterns' works (and what initially was the motivation to not implement this). And enabling search in some other buffers is indeed out of scope.\nTo hunt for TODOs in a project, I'd use a good old grepping: either with MiniPick.builtin.grep() or MiniPick.builtin.grep_live().",
